ipant was 110 years old  almost knock on wood right so um you  know their experience has you know  generally within that group even is is  very diverse  but i think it's the idea especially of  socially assisted robots that they are  they're natural in their communication  and interaction  capabilities so there's no  knowledge that has to be gained to use  the technology because you interact with  the robot the same way you would  interact with a person  and we found that that's important and  of course the generations to come will  be easier and easier when we get to the  gaming generation right so um i think  that's important uh it's it's important  to pre you know to present the  technology make sure that people  understand what its needs and wants are  and you're matching the needs and wants  of the users  and you know you deploy it so that they  can understand  why they need it why it has long-term  benefits which is another thing a lot of  studies have been short-term you take  probably you know you were discussing  you know pilot studies are only for a  certain number of months and then the  robots are taken out and then it's kind  of what's going to happen next right  so we need to make sure that we ensure  that we have this long-term deployment  to gain the benefits of using the  technology and the technology needs to  adapt to people in the field so that's  why the intelligence of a robot is  really important and brings together  this ai and robotics together why  these two fields coming together  actually  improve our technology deployment  so there's a there's a question  that that's come in um we typically  think about  robotics automation as  a threat uh to jobs and job security uh  but this person wants to know how can  robots help us with the emerging hr  um or healthcare hr crisis  [Music]  so  it's um this is a really important  question  uh what is quite clear uh is that  actually both things might be true that  robots could be a threat  in terms 